## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`AlertStudioPage`** SwiftUI surface at parity with the 2342-line web source `features/notifications/pages/AlertStudioPage.tsx` — **22 files, ~5,900 LOC** at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/AlertStudioPage.*` (commit `e5bd28357`).

**What was built (full parity):** page chrome + actions; gated AI builder/conflict/tuning composition slots (baseline = off, ADR-015 §I3); templates browser (47 curated rule templates + derived signal catalog, search, category filter, card grid); responsive two-column rules-list + the complete typed-rule editor (name/status, vehicle targeting, signal+operator OR computed-metric panel, severity + allowed-ops, the kind-aware typed-value editor, cooldown + alert-behavior force-choose with recommendation banner, repeat-only max-fires + escalation, message template + include-title, test-delivery channel picker, Save/Delete/Test/Reset); snooze sheet; discard/delete confirmations. Every state (loading/empty/error/stale/offline/content) renders. All 17 data hooks bind through Shared-free P1/S8 seams (no HTTP in the view); P1/S10 i18n facade (zero hardcoded English); P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry; VoiceOver labels throughout.

**Verification — surface gates all GREEN:**
- Isolated SwiftPM harness (Swift 6 language mode, complete strict concurrency) compiling the exact shipped sources against the **real** generated design tokens: `swift build` 0 errors/0 warnings; **56 XCTest cases pass, 0 failures**
- Real-SDK `swiftc -typecheck`: **iOS 18 = 0**, **macOS 15 = 0**
- `swiftlint --strict`: **0 violations** (21 files) · `swiftformat --lint`: **0/21** · `check-placeholders`: **COUNT=0** (10 verbatim-parity opt-outs)
- KMP `Shared.xcframework` assembled (`GRADLE_SHARED_EXIT=0`); xcodegen enumerates all 22 files

**Full-app xcodebuild gate — honestly DEFERRED** (`IOS_EXIT=65` / `MAC_EXIT=65`), with concrete proof both blockers are pre-existing and unrelated to this surface: iOS is a swift-frontend **IRGen crash uniquely in `AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift`** (a sibling file I never touched — **zero `error:` diagnostics, zero AlertStudioPage errors**); macOS fails at **dev-signing validation before any compilation**. This matches the repo's sanctioned "code-complete + DEFERRED Xcode gate" disposition. Log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.



